lesson k-dissolving-and-sieving v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=4 subject=chemistry levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Mixing and getting it back"
  goal "Say which things dissolve in water and which do not, and use a sieve to get big things out of small."

  look {
    scene 30x12 {
      row jars at=canvas(1, 1) space=3 align=end {
        mixture one things=["sand"] water=1 names=1
        mixture two things=["sugar"] water=1 names=1
      }
    }
    say """
      Stir sand into water and it sinks to the bottom where you can see it. Stir sugar in and it
      dissolves: it spreads through the water so you cannot see it, but it is still there, and the
      water tastes sweet. A sieve keeps big things like pebbles and lets small things like sand fall
      through.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.can-you-see-it x="sand" level=medium
    }
    practice k.can-you-see-it count=3 seed=2 easy-count=1 hard-count=2
    practice k.which-dissolved count=2 seed=3
    practice k.sieve-stays count=2 seed=4 easy-count=1
    show k.sugar-in-water
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.sieve-sugar
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.sieve-or-water k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  remember {
    say "Sugar and salt dissolve. Sand does not. A sieve keeps the big things."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud. Two clear glasses, warm water, a spoon of sugar and a spoon of sand
    are the whole lesson, and tasting is allowed for the sugar only. The wrong idea to watch is that
    dissolved sugar has gone; let the child taste. If the child is stuck on the sieve, shake a
    kitchen sieve of rice and flour together. Off the page, sieve flour for a cake and look at what
    stays behind. China, 3-6岁儿童学习与发展指南 (learning and development guide for children aged 3
    to 6), 科学探究 (recalled, not fetched): "能用多种感官或动作去探索物体" (Explore objects with several
    senses and movements.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level sand is worked in the teacher's pen first, the things to stir are sugar and sand, and pebbles are sieved from sand."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the things to stir are salt and cork, flour and pebbles stand beside the salt, and the sieves keep rice and peas."
  }
}
